---
/** The cookie policy: everything the site stores in the browser. */
import { href } from '@/shared/lib/href';
import { PUBLISHER } from '../../data/facts';
import { STORED_ITEMS } from '../../data/storage';
import LegalDocument from '../LegalDocument.astro';
---

<LegalDocument title="Cookie policy" subtitle="Politique de cookies" updated="2026-11-04">
  <p>
    <strong>This site sets no cookies and uses no trackers</strong>: no analytics, no advertising,
    no social media buttons, and no content loaded from other sites. It does keep a few preferences
    in your browser’s storage so the pages look and behave the way you left them. They are listed
    below in full.
  </p>

  <h2 id="rules">The rules</h2>
  <p>
    Under article 82 of the French <em>loi Informatique et Libertés</em>, which transposes the
    ePrivacy Directive, storing or reading information on your device needs your prior consent,
    unless it is strictly necessary for a service you asked for. The CNIL counts among these
    exceptions items that only remember choices you made about how a site is displayed. Everything
    this site stores falls in that category, so it asks for no consent and shows no banner. If a
    non-essential cookie or tracker is ever added, it will only be set after you accept it, with an
    option to refuse that is as easy as accepting, and a way to change your mind later.
  </p>

  <h2 id="inventory">What is stored</h2>
  <p>
    All items are <strong>first-party</strong> (written and read only by this site) and{' '}
    <strong>essential</strong>. None of them identifies you, and none is ever sent to a server: they
    stay in your browser.
  </p>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th scope="col">Name</th>
        <th scope="col">Type</th>
        <th scope="col">Purpose</th>
        <th scope="col">Set</th>
        <th scope="col">Duration</th>
        <th scope="col">Party</th>
        <th scope="col">Category</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      {STORED_ITEMS.map((item) => (
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Name">
            <code>{item.name}</code>
          </td>
          <td data-label="Type">{item.storage}</td>
          <td data-label="Purpose">{item.purpose}</td>
          <td data-label="Set">{item.set}</td>
          <td data-label="Duration">{item.duration}</td>
          <td data-label="Party">First-party</td>
          <td data-label="Category">Essential</td>
        </tr>
      ))}
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p>The site uses no cookies, IndexedDB databases, service workers or offline caches.</p>

  <h2 id="read">Information read from your device</h2>
  <p>
    The home and download pages read your browser’s description of your system (its user agent and,
    in Chromium-based browsers, its platform and processor architecture) to suggest the right
    installer. This happens only in your browser: nothing is stored or sent, and the page still
    lists every file if it can’t tell.
  </p>
  <p>
    Like any website, this one is served by a hosting provider that receives your IP address and
    browser details with each request. That isn’t a cookie, and the{' '}
    <a href={href('/privacy/')}>privacy policy</a> explains it.
  </p>

  <h2 id="links">Links to other sites</h2>
  <p>
    Links to GitHub and other sites load nothing until you follow them. Once you do, that site’s own
    cookie policy applies.
  </p>

  <h2 id="control">Seeing and clearing what is stored</h2>
  <p>
    You can check this list yourself in your browser’s developer tools (<strong>Application</strong>
    → <strong>Storage</strong> in Chrome and Edge, <strong>Storage</strong> in Firefox and Safari).
    To remove the items, clear this site’s data in your browser settings, or browse in a private
    window. The site works the same without them; it just forgets your choices.
  </p>

  <h2 id="contact">Questions</h2>
  <p>
    Write to <a href={`mailto:${PUBLISHER.email}`}>{PUBLISHER.email}</a>.
  </p>
</LegalDocument>
